# 16. Worker packaging and installation

Do not require a full Orion server installation on the endpoint merely to run the worker.

Produce lightweight worker install artifacts from the same source commit/version:

```text
orion-worker-<version>-windows-x64.zip
orion-worker-<version>-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
```

Exact naming may follow current release conventions.

Worker bundle requirements:
- native Windows/Linux;
- Python 3.12+ may remain a prerequisite in v1;
- no Node/npm;
- no Orion UI;
- no E5 model provisioning;
- no model runtime requirement;
- only worker/runtime dependencies;
- worker config example;
- install/uninstall/update-safe launcher behavior;
- paths with spaces on Windows;
- checksums/manifest tied to exact source SHA;
- no secrets in archive.

Existing full Orion release bundles remain valid and must not regress.

If a separate Python distribution/package is the cleanest way to avoid pulling server-only dependencies, create it deliberately; do not copy large source trees or install editable source on the endpoint.

